sentences.i:
Time has softened toward my plight * and pitied my long-burning grief;
it has given me my desire * and taken away what I feared.
So I will forgive it the sins * it committed in the past:
for the wolf has no escape * from a ruin that will destroy him,
and the vineyard is mine alone, * with no fool to share it.

sentences.l:
Live by the deceit, for you (are) in * a time whose sons (are) like the lions of Bīsha;
and turn the spear-shaft of the cunning until * the millstone of the livelihood turns;
and pluck the fruits, and if they-escape- * -you, [content] yourself with the herbage.

sentences.i:
Live by deceit, for you live in * an age whose children are the lions of Bīsha;
turn cunning's spear-shaft round and round * until the mill of your living turns;
pluck the fruit, and if it slips * your grasp, content yourself with grass.”
